---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import TimeLine from "../components/cv/TimeLine.astro";
---

<BaseLayout sideBarActiveItemID="journey" title="Journey | Agueda Schwartz" description="From education research in Lima to building 0-to-1 AI products in the US. Career timeline, education, and certifications.">
  <div class="pb-8 mt-5">
    <div class="text-lg opacity-75">
      From education research in Lima to building 0-to-1 AI products in the US. Here's how I got here.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold mb-5">Experience</div>

    <TimeLine
      title="Product Manager, WGU Labs"
      subtitle="Sep 2022 to Present | Remote"
    >
      A five-person team had stalled on an AI portfolio, and when they were reassigned I was told to carry it with AI instead, with fractional support from a UX researcher and an engineer. I built the operating system I ran it on, took the work from discovery through an evidence-based pivot to a 12-week pilot, and tested our own AI product hard enough to publish what it could not do. Leadership wrapped it in June 2026.
    </TimeLine>

    <TimeLine
      title="Senior to Lead Learning Experience Designer, WGU Labs"
      subtitle="Jun 2021 to Sep 2022 | Remote"
    >
      A public research university was moving its nursing programs to competency-based education and nobody had worked out how far they had to go. I mapped all 93 courses against a new national framework of ten domains, quantified the gaps, and used Universal Design for Learning to build the train-of-trainers series that carried about 40 faculty through the change. Promoted from Senior to Lead in 15 months.
    </TimeLine>

    <TimeLine
      title="Learning and Development Specialist, Berdon LLP"
      subtitle="Jun 2020 to Jun 2021 | New York, NY"
    >
      A 200+ module professional education library served accountants, partners and tax attorneys, and every year tax law changed enough to make parts of it wrong. I owned the annual refresh and the standard the whole library was held to, and I grew from supporting the subject-matter-expert partnerships to running them. I also contributed to a firm-wide compliance tracker that confirmed license renewals across three training channels.
    </TimeLine>

    <TimeLine
      title="Product Owner, Innova Schools"
      subtitle="Nov 2017 to Jul 2018 | Lima, Peru"
    >
      Leadership asked for reporting dashboards. Talking to users showed the ask was not the need: the problem was upstream, in how data got entered under deadline. I cut the dashboard and shipped a data-entry tool that saved automatically and worked offline. Input errors fell 30% across 30,000 transactions and task time fell 10%. With 2,000 daily users across 20+ locations, I ran train-of-trainers through five people so the rollout did not depend on me.
    </TimeLine>

    <TimeLine
      title="Monitoring and Evaluation Manager, Innova Schools"
      subtitle="Mar 2016 to Oct 2017 | Lima, Peru"
    >
      Four learning platforms were running across 20+ locations with no agreed way to judge them, Khan Academy among them. I designed the evaluations, tracking adoption, completion and frequency of use alongside learning outcomes, because usage is not comprehension. My recommendations were the evidence leadership used to decide what to scale and what to shut off.
    </TimeLine>

    <TimeLine
      title="Monitoring and Evaluation Coordinator, Innova Schools"
      subtitle="Mar 2014 to Feb 2016 | Lima, Peru"
    >
      There was no agreed methodology for assessing the network's innovation pilots. I helped a small team build one with learning outcomes as the primary criterion, and it became the starting point for the platform evaluations I later owned. I coordinated field data collectors and moderated the qualitative research myself, in Spanish: observation, interviews and focus groups.
    </TimeLine>

    <TimeLine
      title="Research Assistant, Pontificia Universidad Católica del Perú"
      subtitle="Jul 2010 to Feb 2014 | Lima, Peru"
    >
      Conducted research on educational technology and digital learning resources.
    </TimeLine>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold mb-5">Education</div>

    <TimeLine
      title="MA, Digital Media Design for Learning"
      subtitle="New York University | 2018 to 2020"
    >
      Digital media, instructional design, and learning science.
    </TimeLine>

    <TimeLine
      title="BA, Educational Psychology"
      subtitle="Pontificia Universidad Católica del Perú | 2005 to 2012"
    >
      Learning theory, cognitive science, and research methodology. The foundation for everything I build.
    </TimeLine>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold mb-5">Certifications</div>

    <TimeLine
      title="Designing Strategy"
      subtitle="IDEO U | 2024"
    >
    </TimeLine>

    <TimeLine
      title="Designing a Business"
      subtitle="IDEO U | 2023"
    >
    </TimeLine>
  </div>

</BaseLayout>
